# INV-01 — invented. A five-over match: the basics, and a chase won with wickets in hand.
# Edge cases: strike rotation on odd runs and at the over's end; a maiden with
# byes and leg byes in it; bowled, caught, lbw, stumped; a wide and a no-ball;
# a free hit hit for four; a wide for four (five wides); a run out of the
# non-striker after a run completed, at the bowler's end; the target reached
# mid-over.
match INV-01
title Five overs, a chase won by eight wickets
date 2026-11-01
overs 5
sides Home Away

innings 1 Home
open B1 B2
over BW1  1 . 4 . 2 1
over BW2  . 1lb . . 2b .
over BW1  W:b 3 . 6 W:c/F4 1
over BW3  wd 2 . nb+1 4 . 1 .
over BW2  1 1 W:lbw 2 . 4

innings 2 Away
open B1 B2
over BW1  4 1 1 . 6 2
over BW2  . W:st/F1 1 4 wd+4 . 1
over BW3  2 W:ro/F6,+1,ns,end=b 3 . 1b 4
over BW1  1 1lb 2

# ── The card, worked by hand from the balls above ──
